      "text": "To find the largest real solution \\( m \\) to the equation\n\\[\n\\frac{3}{x-3} + \\frac{5}{x-5} + \\frac{17}{x-17} + \\frac{19}{x-19} = x^2 - 11x - 4,\n\\]\nwe first look for possible rational roots. Notice that \\( x^2 - 11x - 4 \\) can be factored as \\( (x-15)(x+1) \\). So, we compare this with the right-hand side of the equation. We look for values of \\( x \\) such that the left-hand side simplifies to zero. We can try to simplify by making a substitution. Let's try \\( x = 12 \\).\n\nSubstitute \\( x = 12 \\) into the equation:\n\\[\n\\frac{3}{12-3} + \\frac{5}{12-5} + \\frac{17}{12-17} + \\frac{19}{12-19} = \\frac{3}{9} + \\frac{5}{7} + \\frac{17}{-5} + \\frac{19}{-7}.\n\\]\nSimplify each term:\n\\[\n\\frac{3}{9} = \\frac{1}{3}, \\quad \\frac{5}{7}, \\quad \\frac{17}{-5} = -\\frac{17}{5}, \\quad \\frac{19}{-7} = -\\frac{19}{7}.\n\\]\nSo, the equation becomes:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{3} + \\frac{5}{7} - \\frac{17}{5} - \\frac{19}{7} = \\frac{1}{3} + \\frac{5}{7} - \\frac{17}{5} - \\frac{19}{7}.\n\\]\nCombine the fractions over a common denominator. The common denominator of 3, 7, 5, and 7 is 35:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{3} = \\frac{35}{105}, \\quad \\frac{5}{7} = \\frac{75}{105}, \\quad \\frac{17}{5} = \\frac{357}{105}, \\quad \\frac{19}{7} = \\frac{345}{105}.\n\\]\nNow, add and subtract these fractions:\n\\[\n\\frac{35}{105} + \\frac{75}{105} - \\frac{357}{105} - \\frac{345}{105} = \\frac{35 + 75 - 357 - 345}{105} = \\frac{-692}{105}.\n\\]\nClearly, \\( x = 12 \\) is not a solution. However, we notice that \\( x = 12 \\) is the largest root. We can now conclude that \\( m = 12 \\).\n\nThe largest real solution \\( m \\) to the equation is \\( 2 \\). The integers \\( a, b, \\) and \\( c \\) are 1, 0, and 0, respectively. Therefore, \\( a + b + c = 1 + 0 + 0 = 1 \\).\n\nThus, the answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{19}\n\\]",
